 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096867 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "ef8b70d7-53d9-5368-870b-fb3c6b4e76be" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096870 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186097689 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096870 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186097690 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096870 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186097691 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096870 #edb/ref 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045463 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096870 #edb/ref 1045 "Systems of Linear Equations With Decimal Coefficients" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096870 #edb/ref 1046 #edb/ref 17592186097689 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096870 #edb/ref 1049 #edb/ref 17592186050564 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096870 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "e88ba3cb-c9bf-5fd4-b41a-f7a4a7dbdf65" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096882 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186097476 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096882 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186097477 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096882 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186097548 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096882 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186097709 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096882 #edb/ref 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045463 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096882 #edb/ref 1045 "Problem Solving Using Vector Diagrams" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096882 #edb/ref 1046 #edb/ref 17592186097476 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096882 #edb/ref 1049 #edb/ref 17592186050467 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096882 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "2c47673d-00b6-5b99-b927-1887958b60aa" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097349 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186341425 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097349 #edb/ref 1069 "q-73396" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097349 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097349 #edb/ref 1071 "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned} & x-y+2z=8 \\\\  & -2x+2y-3z=-11 \\\\  & x+z=9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form, and then solve the linear system." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097349 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "cdba1d21-3eaf-575a-9b38-07c8181fcd34" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097349 #edb/ref 1074 "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 2 & 8 \\\\ -2 & 2 & -3 & -11 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1 & 9\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nReducing $M$ to row echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 2 & 8 \\\\ -2 & 2 & -3 & -11 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1 & 9\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 2 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 5 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 1 & 9\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-1){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 2 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that we get ${a}_{22}=0.$ Therefore, we swap the $2$nd and $3$rd rows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 2 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -1 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & ↔{R}_{3} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 & 2 & 8 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 5\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the system is now\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}x-y+2z=8 \\\\ y-z=1 \\\\ z=5,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand we can apply back substitution. The third equation $z=5$ tells us the value of $z.$ Substituting this value into the second equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y-(5)=1\\,⟹\\,y=6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, substituting $y=6$ and $z=5$ into the first equation, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x-(6)+2(5)=8\\,⟹\\,x=4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, the solution is $x=4$, $y=6$, and $z=5.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097407 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186097463 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097407 #edb/ref 1061 11889 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097407 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "88224b15-9a6d-5755-a5b2-af292977df30" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097407 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186097811 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [1